WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.399
Image compression explained, with a slider you can drag.

2
00:00:05.899 --> 00:00:09.936
Lossy, lossless, JPG, WebP and AVIF in plain words.

3
00:00:09.936 --> 00:00:15.477
Drag the slider to see what quality settings actually do to a picture.

4
00:00:17.728 --> 00:00:22.144
Lossless and lossy. Lossless compression keeps every pixel exactly.

5
00:00:24.294 --> 00:00:29.812
Drag the slider. The image below is drawn in your browser and encoded with

6
00:00:29.812 --> 00:00:32.870
your browser's own JPG and WebP encoders.

7
00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:39.547
Resize before you compress. The biggest saving is often not the quality

8
00:00:39.547 --> 00:00:40.503
setting at all.

9
00:00:42.653 --> 00:00:45.784
To try it, open Image Compressor in OpenFile.

10
00:00:45.784 --> 00:00:49.750
Drop in a file, adjust the settings and press the button.

11
00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:53.299
It all runs on your device, so nothing is uploaded.

12
00:00:55.753 --> 00:00:59.700
Read the full post, with live demos, on the OpenFile blog.
